    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27-a3">

                <pb facs="0106" n="32" xml:id="pg32"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. de Thile to Mr. Wright.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 23, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Francis Benndorf, in whose favor you
                    interceded in your communication under date of 16th May, 1866, received in the
                    fall of 1862 a simple permit, valuable for eight days, to go to Leipsic. Instead
                    of returning at the expiration of this document, he went to America, whence he
                    returned during the present year. His unauthorized absence having lasted only 3¼
                    years, he, according to the law of 31st December, 1842, retained his Prussian
                    nationality. He should, therefore, fulfil his military obligations, and I regret
                    exceedingly that I cannot obtain permission for him to leave the army.</p>
                <p>I take this occasion to renew assurances, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THILE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>., <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >&amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
